e-owned collateral forfeited from its pawn activities or merchandise purchased from customers. It also provides web-based applications, including EZ+ that allow customers to manage its pawn transactions, layaways, and loyalty rewards online. In addition, the company offers advance cash collateralized by tangible personal property, such as jewelry, consumer electronics, tools, sporting goods or musical instruments. It operates its pawn shops under the EZPAWN, Value Pawn & Jewelry, Empe\u00f1o F\u00e1cil, Cash Apoyo Efectivo, GuatePrenda, MaxiEfectivo, La Familia Pawn, and Jewelry and CashWiz brands. EZCORP, Inc. was incorporated in 1989 and is headquartered in Austin, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Lachlan P. Given BBus | CEO & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $2.7M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $173K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $14K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 16\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["EZCORP, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.5B market cap on $1.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +17% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically. Gross margins of 59% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $141M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.12\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 7.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.7%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.5% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (28.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 15% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.4M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3380891.53},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 57% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 29% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"44,433 EZCORP, Inc. $EZPW Shares Purchased by Stephens Investment Management Group LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/44433-ezcorp-inc-ezpw-shares-purchased-by-stephens-investment-management-group-llc.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795